To implement a Binary Search Tree (BST) to display the inorder traversal sequence and identify the kth smallest element by performing the following operations:
Insert elements into the BST.
Accept the value of k from the user.
Display all elements in ascending order using inorder traversal.
Count the visited nodes and identify the position of the kth smallest element.
Display the inorder sequence, position, and value of the selected element.
Each node contains an integer data value.
